The fitting method does not always reproduce the results of the integration method, especially for high transverse associated momenta it often undershoots those values. One source of disagreement could be the shape of near- and away-side peaks, which are not necessarily Gaussian as assumed in the fit function. It has also been observed that the determination of a background from a sparsely populated histogram does not yield reliable results. A last problem with the fitting method is of technical nature: the fit does not always converge, making it an uncomfortable choice for automated yield extraction.

